WEBVTT

NOTE
Fictional reference data for the eval set; all names are placeholders.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:09.000
<v [PERSON_1]>Thanks all. Today we want to understand the garment flows at [SITE].

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:22.000
<v [PERSON_2]>I'm the logistics director at [CUSTOMER], a fashion retailer with two hundred and ten stores and a growing web shop. [SITE] serves both.

3
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v [PERSON_2]>We want a pocket sorter for hanging garments, about twelve thousand pockets, buffering store orders and sequencing web orders by customer.

4
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:48.000
<v [PERSON_2]>Returns are huge for the web shop, around thirty-five percent. Returned items must be inspected, re-tagged and back in stock within twenty-four hours.

5
00:00:48.500 --> 00:01:01.000
<v [PERSON_3]>IT. Every garment carries an RFID tag. We want tunnel readers at goods-in and at the store dispatch so we never count by hand again.

6
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:14.000
<v [PERSON_3]>Our merchandising system allocates stock to stores overnight. The interface to the new system has not been designed; our merchandising vendor quotes six months for any change.

7
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:25.000
<v [PERSON_2]>Peak is the four weeks before Christmas and the January sale. We do not know yet how big the web share will be next year; marketing is still planning.

8
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:35.000
<v [PERSON_4]>Facilities. The pocket sorter would go on a new mezzanine. We have not decided whether we build it or you include it in your scope.
